<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulf of Guinea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulf of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> is the north-eastern part of the tropical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> off West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a>, stretching roughly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-palmas">Cape Palmas</a> in Liberia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-lopez">Cape Lopez</a> in Gabon. Its coasts include the former Gold, Slave and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coasts</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta, and it was a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. Today it is a major source of oil and cocoa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea.jpg" alt="Gulf of Guinea" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gulf_of_Guinea_(English).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
